The assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md, but it is not committed. session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so git add refused the file and the || true hid the failure. I didn't force-add it. Earlier "assessment" commits exist, so the harness probably commits the file itself.

What matters most for planning:
• Delete the two Day-247 stopgaps. yoagent 0.26.7 is now in Cargo.lock (bot commit 5124a587). It ships ModelConfig::claude_sonnet_4_6() and ModelConfig::preset("bedrock"|"openrouter", id). Those replace:
  • the hand-written Sonnet 4.6 arm at agent_builder.rs:799 (#1123)
  • providers::bedrock_anthropic_preset_id at providers.rs:213 (#1124)

  @yuanhao said on #1122 at 13:16 that deleting them is still my job. Three differences have to be decided in the task, not assumed:
  • Bedrock ids: my stopgap accepts any lowercase region prefix and strips any -vN:M suffix. yoagent only knows 9 prefixes and a fixed id table, so some ids my stopgap maps will stop mapping.
  • Prices: yoagent's Bedrock and OpenRouter presets come with no price, on purpose. /cost pricing has to stay on yoyo's side (bedrock_region.rs, format/cost.rs:100,470), or those runs will start showing up unpriced.
  • Endpoint: yoagent's Bedrock preset hard-codes us-east-1. yoyo should copy only the limits and reasoning settings, and keep the user's own URL.
• Every task file now needs a `Dependency:` line. The creator added this to evolve.sh today, and the evaluator fails a diff that rebuilds the feature its line names.
• Size gates:
  • config.rs is 11 lines from the FATAL cap. Going past it fails the test suite, and the whole task gets reverted.
  • commands_risk_unhittable.rs is 14 lines from the cap and isn't on the exceptions list.
• Avoid the prompt code: it took 5 of the last 10 self-driven changes. #1129 (yoyo review --quik reads the typo as a file name, reproduced) and the 8 remaining verbs on #1127 are both outside it.

